---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import CephCapacityCalculator from '../../../components/tools/CephCapacityCalculator.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Ceph Capacity Calculator | InfraOpsX"
  description="Estimate Ceph raw and usable capacity, data efficiency, redundancy overhead, and reserve headroom for replicated and erasure-coded layouts."
  lang="en"
  canonicalPath="/tools/ceph-capacity-calculator/"
  enPath="/tools/ceph-capacity-calculator/"
  zhPath="/zh/tools/ceph-capacity-calculator/"
>
  <Header locale="en" switchHref="/zh/tools/ceph-capacity-calculator/" />

  <main class="tool-detail-shell">
    <div class="container tool-detail-container">
      <div class="tools-breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <a href="/tools/">Tools</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span>Ceph Capacity Calculator</span>
      </div>

      <header class="tool-detail-header">
        <span class="section-label">CEPH · CAPACITY PLANNING</span>
        <h1>Ceph Capacity Calculator</h1>
        <p>Estimate raw capacity, theoretical usable capacity, and reserve headroom for a Ceph cluster.</p>
      </header>

      <section class="tool-section" aria-labelledby="calculator-heading">
        <div class="tool-section-heading">
          <span class="section-label">CALCULATOR</span>
          <h2 id="calculator-heading">Plan Ceph capacity before deployment.</h2>
        </div>
        <CephCapacityCalculator locale="en" />
      </section>

      <section class="tool-info-grid">
        <article class="tool-info-card">
          <span class="section-label">HOW IT WORKS</span>
          <h2>Use the layout that matches your data protection model.</h2>
          <p>For replicated storage, theoretical usable capacity is the raw capacity divided by the replication size. For erasure-coded storage, usable capacity is based on the data-to-total-shard ratio <code>k / (k + m)</code>. Recommended usable capacity is calculated after applying the configured reserve percentage.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="tool-info-card">
          <span class="section-label">IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS</span>
          <h2>Capacity planning is an estimate.</h2>
          <p>Actual available space can also be affected by BlueStore overhead, metadata, uneven OSD sizes, CRUSH rules and failure domains, recovery and backfill headroom, and current cluster utilization. This estimate is not the same as the capacity reported by Ceph <code>df</code>.</p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="tool-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
        <span class="section-label">FAQ</span>
        <h2 id="faq-heading">Common questions</h2>
        <details open>
          <summary>What is the difference between TB and TiB?</summary>
          <p>TB uses decimal units: 1 TB = 10<sup>12</sup> bytes. TiB uses binary units: 1 TiB = 2<sup>40</sup> bytes. The calculator keeps your selected unit as the primary display and shows the corresponding decimal or binary unit as a reference.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does the recommended usable capacity equal the available capacity reported by Ceph?</summary>
          <p>No. It is a planning estimate that applies your reserve percentage to theoretical usable capacity. BlueStore, metadata, topology, recovery behavior and utilization can make the actual Ceph result different.</p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section class="related-tools">
        <div>
          <span class="section-label">RELATED TOOLS</span>
          <h2>More infrastructure tools are on the way.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/tools/">View all tools</a>
      </section>

      <section class="tool-cta">
        <div class="cta-box">
          <div>
            <span class="section-label">INFRAOPSX</span>
            <h2>Need help with Ceph or Kubernetes storage?</h2>
            <p>Contact InfraOpsX for practical infrastructure guidance.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact InfraOpsX</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer locale="en" />
</BaseLayout>
